    "created_at": "2023-10-25T09:34:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-25T09:34:40Z",
    "body": "This is brilliant and exactly what I needed this for. I find coming up with my own colors via hex a bit overwhelming so prefer to have a \"standard\" set I can pick from. I've used this feature to configure the [140 standard named html colors](https://www.w3schools.com/colors/colors_groups.asp) for use in starship so I can just pick from the site and use the names (e.g. 'deepskyblue').\r\n\r\n[gist link](https://gist.github.com/fossrob/7c780bf65b3ab00f8712ae0f168d660e)\r\n",
